-- The wrap (w2): the deck is a ring; wrapping is modular index arithmetic, and no row ever moves. Twin of 122-wrap.bqn. (was w2-wrap)
-- The classic trick: hang a modifier at the deck's end to catch the first slot. The deck is a ring, the rotation is arithmetic, and no card ever changes rows.
-- Wand [SB, DP] with the cast pointer at slot 1: the block draws DP, needs one more, and wraps to the front — the classic trick that hangs a modifier at the buffer's end to catch the first slot.
-- DrawPos is modular position arithmetic. Bal scans in the tie-free draw order and scatters back by inverse grade. The modifier at the end then binds to the first slot.
--! registry ../registries/122-wrap.reg
--! expect drawPos = 0 1 0
--! expect bal = 0 0 1
--! expect damage = 0 13 0

Spell , DrawPos = (Slot - 1) % 2
Spell , Bal = 1 + (scan(+) (DrawAdd - 1) along rot)
Spell & Proj & DrawPos == 1 , Damage += 10
